{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/6525","createdAt":"2026-10-05T04:57:06Z","decision":"accept_compat_change","decisionDigest":"sha256:3391b64f477332cb8e892081fb29e68813ed21b74e04bdf2d586ddcb2685870b","decisionId":"rdec-55f30ed0ad55eba70152d17bcfbe049a","findingId":"cf-39627352fe66ab9c","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:7ec985a58e2db8055ea503bb0b3ce4c09d0242888de1dbce52e14705da0422db","packageIdentity":"epkg-9d30a2222cfc5e8c6fd171ab8c9e260339583caa606c48f34347adb81f4ac47c","prNumber":"6525","reason":"Not intended (narrow regression, reported to the author in our review): a whole-line // comment indented with a non-ASCII space (NBSP, U+3000, U+2028, vertical tab, form feed) or preceded by a byte order mark used to be removed together with that character, because the old ^\\s*// regex matched it; the scanner keeps the character, JSON.parse accepts only ASCII whitespace, and the file contributes 0 rows instead of 1. In the shell, Quickshell's FileView drops a BOM at the very start of a file, so the case that empties the menu is the indented comment line. Copying any \\s character outside a string as a plain space would keep the old behaviour.","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
